      "particles": 4
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weights and activations sit across the 4 HBM3e stacks (96 GiB, 2.9 TB/s per chip).",
      "focus": ["hbm-dram-die0", "hbm-dram-die1", "hbm-base-die0", "hbm-base-die1"],
      "dot": "hbm-dram-die0",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "hbm"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. A DMA engine on the local die reads the HBM stacks attached to it.",
      "focus": ["dma-engine-die0"],
      "dot": "dma-engine-die0",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. If the needed tile lives in the other die's HBM, it crosses the ABF substrate die-to-die link.",
      "focus": ["die-link"],
      "dot": "die-link",
      "stage": "die-to-die"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. The Descriptor Generation Engine (DGE) schedules an asynchronous DMA copy of the A/B tiles into SBUF.",
      "focus": ["dge"],
      "dot": "dge",
      "drill": "neuroncore-detail",
      "stage": "tma"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. Tiles sit in SBUF (28 MiB on-chip SRAM per NeuronCore), ready for the Tensor Engine.",
      "focus": ["sbuf"],
      "dot": "sbuf",
      "drill": "neuroncore-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. The Tensor Engine loads the stationary operand into its 128×128 PE array; the moving operand streams through and multiplies every cycle.",
      "focus": ["tensor-engine"],
      "dot": "tensor-engine",
      "drill": "neuroncore-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. Partial sums accumulate in PSUM (2 MiB), not in general registers. Steps 4–7 repeat along the contraction dimension.",
      "focus": ["psum"],
      "dot": "psum",
      "drill": "neuroncore-detail",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Epilogue: the Vector and Scalar Engines apply bias, activation and casts; GpSimd handles any custom op the other engines can't.",
      "focus": ["vector-engine", "scalar-engine", "gpsimd-engine"],
      "dot": "vector-engine",
      "drill": "neuroncore-detail",
      "stage": "epilogue"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Results DMA back to HBM; with tensor parallelism, NeuronLink-v3 (1.28 TB/s) and the CC-Cores all-reduce across chips.",
      "focus": ["neuronlink-die0"],
      "dot": "neuronlink-die0",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    }
  ],
